-- title:
--   Level-q automorphisms stabilise residually transcendental valuation subrings
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ and a positive integer $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$, and a prime $\ell$ with $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell \mid M'$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic $0$ and $\zeta \in L$ a primitive $q$-th root of unity; the hypothesis `hι` provides a ring homomorphism $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota\zeta = e^{2\pi i/q}$. Let $H_1 \le (\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times$ be, by `hH₁`, the intersection of [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH q M'`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22) — the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$ — with the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/\ell)^\times$. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L \subseteq L((t))$ which, by `hK`, is [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') H₁)`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103): the $L$-subfield of the Laurent series field generated by the image under [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) of the $q$-expansion function field of $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$ over $\mathbb{Q}$. Let $A$ be a henselian discrete valuation ring which is an $A$-algebra inside $L$ with $L$ as its fraction field, with algebraically closed residue field, with $q \in \mathfrak{m}_A$ and with $\zeta$ in the image of $A \to L$, and let $K$ be an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$. Let $j \in K$ be the element whose Laurent expansion is [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81), the $q$-expansion of the modular invariant $j$, with $j \ne 0$. Let $\varpi$ generate $\mathfrak{m}_A$ (`hϖ`) and let $\varpi_t \in A$ satisfy $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1} = q u$ with $u \in A^\times$ (`hϖt`).
--
--   Write $C :=$ `chartAlgFin A K j` for the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ consisting of the elements integral over $A[j]$, and `jChartFin A K j` for $j$ regarded as an element of $C$. Let $y \subset C$ be a maximal ideal (`hy`) containing the image of $\varpi$ (`hϖy`) which is supersingular in the sense of `hss`: for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi : C \to \Omega$ with kernel $y$, the value $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), the set of those $\jmath \in \Omega$ such that every elliptic curve over $\Omega$ with $j$-invariant $\jmath$ has no nonzero point killed by $q$.
--
--   The hypothesis `hArig` (the Drinfeld chart witness, seven clauses, summarised here) asserts the following for every point $z$ of the two-chart integral model $X :=$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) (the pushout glueing $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the $j$-finite and $j^{-1}$-finite chart algebras), provided the germ at $z$ of the image of $\varpi$ under the structure morphism `toBase` to $\operatorname{Spec} A$ lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk, and provided a point $y'$ of `XFin A K j` $= \operatorname{Spec} C$ maps to $z$ under the canonical morphism `ιFin` and satisfies the same supersingularity condition as $y$ for $y'$`.asIdeal`: there exist a complete discrete valuation ring $W$, a ring homomorphism $\sigma : A \to W$ with $\mathfrak{m}_W = (\sigma\varpi)$, power series $f, u, v \in W[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u, v$ units and $f \equiv X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1 \pmod{(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}}$ (the Drinfeld form [`DrinfeldCurve.LocalChart.drinfeldForm q W`](def/DrinfeldCurve_LocalChart.html#L18)), and a ring isomorphism $e$ from the adic completion of the stalk of $X$ at $z$ onto $S := W[[X_0,X_1]]/(C(\sigma(\varpi_t^{q+1}))v - fu)$, such that: (i) $e$ carries the germ of each $a \in A$ to the class of $C(\sigma a)$; (ii) for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, every $\tau : K \simeq_L K$ with [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.IsLevelAutAt L q ζ q (q ^ 2 * M') H₁ γ⁻¹ K τ`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelLevelAutAt.html#L29) maps $C$ into $C$; (iii) for such $\gamma$ with $\gamma_{11} \equiv 1 \pmod \ell$, the restriction of $\tau$ to $C$ is congruent to the identity modulo $y'$`.asIdeal`; (iv) for each such $\gamma$ and $\tau$ which is residually trivial at $y'$ there are a ring automorphism $\theta$ of $S$, a scalar $c \in W$ and a matrix $M \in M_2(W)$ with $\theta$ implementing the action of $\tau$ through $e$ and the germ map $C \to$ stalk, $\theta$ fixing the constants, $\theta(X_{jj})$ congruent to $\sum_{ii} M_{ii\,jj}X_{ii}$ modulo the square of the ideal generated by the classes of $X_0, X_1$, $c^{q+1} \equiv 1$ and $M \equiv c\,\gamma$ modulo $\mathfrak{m}_W$, $c \equiv 1$ whenever $\gamma_{11} \equiv 1 \pmod \ell$, and $c \not\equiv 1$ whenever $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau \neq \mathrm{id}$; (v) a branch-separation clause: two primes $P_1, P_2$ of $S$ not containing both classes of $X_0, X_1$, containing the class of $C(\sigma\varpi)$, and containing linear forms $a_iX_0 + b_iX_1$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^2$ with $q \nmid a_1b_2 - a_2b_1$, have distinct contractions to the stalk along $e$ composed with the completion map; (vi) for a prime $P$ of $S$ of this kind whose linear form may be taken to be $X_0$, and for $a \in C$, the germ of $a$ lies in the contraction of $P$ along $e$ if and only if every Laurent coefficient of $a$ lies in the image of $\mathfrak{m}_A$; (vii) [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L q`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) (the $j$-expansion over $L$ with exponents scaled by $q$) lies in $K$ and in $C$, and for a suitable $a_0 \in A$ with the difference in $y'$`.asIdeal`, an $e_0 \ge 1$ and $h \in (X_0,X_1)^{e_0}$ whose degree-$e_0$ form is non-degenerate in the sense that $\sum_{i} \operatorname{coeff}_{X_0^iX_1^{e_0-i}}(h)\,a^ib^{e_0-i}$ is a unit whenever $a$ or $b$ is a unit of $W$ and $a^qb - ab^q \in \mathfrak{m}_W$, the image of that difference under $e$ composed with the completion and germ maps is the class of $h$.
--
--   A particular such datum is then fixed: a point $z$ of $X$ with the germ $\varpi_z$ of $\varpi$ described as above and lying in the maximal ideal of the stalk, a point $y'$ of $\operatorname{Spec} C$ above $z$ satisfying the supersingularity condition, with $y'$`.asIdeal` $= y$ (`hy'y`), together with a complete discrete valuation ring $W_1$, $\sigma_1 : A \to W_1$ with $\mathfrak{m}_{W_1} = (\sigma_1\varpi)$, series $f_1, u_1, v_1$ with $u_1, v_1$ units and $f_1$ congruent to the Drinfeld form modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$, and an isomorphism $e_1$ from the completed stalk at $z$ onto $S_1 := W_1[[X_0,X_1]]/(C(\sigma_1(\varpi_t^{q+1}))v_1 - f_1u_1)$; the hypothesis `hW₁` asserts for this datum exactly the seven clauses (i)–(vii) listed above.
--
--   Further data: an ideal $J \subseteq C$ which, by `hJ`, is the infimum of the ideals obtained, as $\gamma$ ranges over $\Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ and $\tau$ over the level automorphisms at $\gamma^{-1}$ preserving $C$, as the pullback along the restriction of $\tau$ to $C$ of the contraction along $e_1 \circ (\text{completion}) \circ (\text{germ at } z)$ of the ideal of $S_1$ generated by the classes of $C(\sigma_1\varpi_t)$, $X_0$ and $X_1$; an $A$-subalgebra $B \subseteq K$ which, by `hB`, is generated over $C$ by all $x \in K$ with $x\varpi_t \in J$; and a valuation subring $W \subseteq K$ containing $B$ (`hBW`).
--
--   These are subject to four groups of hypotheses. `hR1`: $C \subseteq B$, and every element of $K$ is a ratio $g/h$ with $g, h \in B$, $h \ne 0$. `hR2`: $A \to B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation, and $B/\varpi B$ has Krull dimension at most $1$. `hR3` (five clauses): $W \cap L$ is the image of $A$; $\mathfrak{m}_W$ is generated by the image of $\varpi$; $W$ is a discrete valuation ring; for $b \in C$, $b \in y$ if and only if $b$ lies in $\mathfrak{m}_W$; and $W$ is the localisation of $B$ at the complement of $\mathfrak{m}_W$, in the sense that $f \in W$ exactly when $f = g/h$ with $g, h \in B$ and $h \notin \mathfrak{m}_W$. `hEQ` (five clauses, summarised here): for every $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$-algebra structure on the residue field $k$ of $A$ there is a surjective ring homomorphism $\rho : B \to$ [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q k`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) (the quotient of $k[X_0,X_1]$ by the ideal generated by `drinfeldPoly q k - 1`) whose kernel is $B \cap \mathfrak{m}_W$, which is compatible with $A \to k$, and which is equivariant for every level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ preserving $W$, through an element $c \in \mathbb{F}_{q^2}^\times$ with $(\text{redQ } q\,\gamma, c)$ in [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276), the kernel of the character $(g,c) \mapsto \det(g)c^{q+1}$, acting by [`DrinfeldCurve.hAction`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L325), and with $c \ne 1$ whenever $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau \ne \mathrm{id}$; every such $\tau$ maps $B$ into $B$; every prime $Q$ of $B$ containing $\varpi$ receives the $\tau$-translate of $B \cap \mathfrak{m}_W$ for some $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ and level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$; an element of $B$ all of whose translates under such $\tau$ lie in $\mathfrak{m}_W$ is divisible by $\varpi$ in $B$; and any level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ which preserves $y$ on $C$ also preserves $W$.
--
--   Here [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.IsLevelAutAt L q ζ q (q ^ 2 * M') H₁ δ K τ`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelLevelAutAt.html#L29) means: for every weight $k$, every pair $f, g$ of modular forms of weight $k$ on $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$ with integral $q$-expansions $p_f, p_g$ and $p_g$ having nonzero image, every $x \in K$ whose Laurent expansion is the image of $p_f/p_g$, and every $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota\zeta = e^{2\pi i/q}$, the series $\iota(\tau x)$ multiplied by the $q$-expansion of $g \mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}\, q\, \delta$ equals the $q$-expansion of $f \mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}\, q\, \delta$, where $\mathrm{conjElemN}\, q\, \delta$ is the matrix with rows $(\delta_{00}, \delta_{01}/q)$ and $(q\delta_{10}, \delta_{11})$.
--
--   Under all these hypotheses the conclusion is a single statement about arbitrary valuation subrings. Let $V$ be a valuation subring of $K$ such that: for $x \in L$, the image of $x$ lies in $V$ exactly when $x$ comes from $A$; the image of $\varpi$ lies in $V$ and in $\mathfrak{m}_V$; every element of $C$ lies in $V$; and there is an element $c \in C$ which is residually transcendental in the sense that for every monic $p \in A[T]$ the value $p(c)$ lies in $V$ and is a unit of $V$. Then for every $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ and every $\tau : K \simeq_L K$ with [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.IsLevelAutAt L q ζ q (q ^ 2 * M') H₁ γ⁻¹ K τ`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelLevelAutAt.html#L29), and every $f \in K$, one has $f \in V$ if and only if $\tau f \in V$; that is, every such $V$ is stable under all level-$\Gamma(q)$ automorphisms in $\Gamma_0(M')$.
--
--   This is the stability statement for Igusa-type valuation subrings in the $\Gamma_1(\ell)$-diamond frame at a supersingular point of the two-chart integral model of the function field of $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$: a valuation subring extending $A$, containing the $j$-finite chart algebra and residually transcendental on it, is invariant under every automorphism of $K$ realising an element of $\Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$. It is used in the construction of the blow-up and end charts and in the comparison of supersingular primes, being cited by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevelOne.exists_endChart_finiteType_isLocalization_pole_of_end_blowupChart_of_drinfeldChartWitness_linked_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevelOne.exists_endChart_finiteType_isLocalization_pole_of_end_blowupChart_of_drinfeldChartWitness_linked_of_dvd), [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevelOne.exists_igusaValuationSubring_translateSep_of_mem_ends_blowupChart_of_drinfeldChartWitness_linked_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevelOne.exists_igusaValuationSubring_translateSep_of_mem_ends_blowupChart_of_drinfeldChartWitness_linked_of_dvd) and [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevelOne.mem_iff_map_mem_isPrime_lt_supersingular_of_isLevelAutAt_gamma_of_drinfeldChartWitness_linked_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevelOne.mem_iff_map_mem_isPrime_lt_supersingular_of_isLevelAutAt_gamma_of_drinfeldChartWitness_linked_of_dvd).
